1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,360
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:05,010
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,010 --> 00:00:06,440
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:07,970
I've worked in a school
cafeteria

5
00:00:07,970 --> 00:00:09,290
for thirty years.

6
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:11,030
Standing on a hard tile
floor,

7
00:00:11,030 --> 00:00:13,010
serving lunch to hundreds
of kids.

8
00:00:13,010 --> 00:00:13,820
I had my right

9
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:15,820
knee replaced two years
ago.

10
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:17,540
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:18,950
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:18,950 --> 00:00:20,120
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:21,470
and it went away.

14
00:00:21,470 --> 00:00:22,560
This is different.

15
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:23,260
Tight.

16
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:23,940
Full.

17
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:25,330
Like a band around the
joint

18
00:00:25,330 --> 00:00:26,720
that never loosens.

19
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:27,900
And for two years I've

20
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:29,160
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:30,660
Give it time.

22
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:32,490
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:34,040
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:35,030
At three months,

25
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:36,050
give it six.

26
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:37,060
At six months,

27
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:38,700
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:39,440
At a year,

29
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:41,320
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:43,300
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:44,700
We went down the list.

32
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,150
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:46,150 --> 00:00:49,050
Every session, every
exercise at home.

34
00:00:49,050 --> 00:00:50,240
I got stronger.

35
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:51,690
The tightness never moved.

36
00:00:51,690 --> 00:00:53,010
The pain pills helped,

37
00:00:53,010 --> 00:00:54,400
and that was the problem.

38
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,190
I'm already on enough
every morning,

39
00:00:56,190 --> 00:00:57,080
and nobody could tell me

40
00:00:57,080 --> 00:00:59,030
when I'd get to stop.

41
00:00:59,030 --> 00:01:00,830
Then a nerve block.

42
00:01:00,830 --> 00:01:03,060
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

43
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:04,060
And after that,

44
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:05,900
a second operation to go
back

45
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,460
in and do it over.

46
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,510
I said no.

47
00:01:08,510 --> 00:01:10,380
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

48
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:11,260
and my knee felt

49
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:13,070
like a band was wrapped
around it,

50
00:01:13,070 --> 00:01:15,610
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

51
00:01:15,610 --> 00:01:17,040
Every morning I took
something

52
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:18,570
for it and went to work.

53
00:01:18,570 --> 00:01:19,880
Couldn't get through one
lunch

54
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:21,840
without leaning on the
steam table,

55
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:23,200
couldn't do the stairs,

56
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:24,350
couldn't stand at the
counter

57
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:25,980
long enough to finish
dinner,

58
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:27,620
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

59
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:29,760
without shifting every two
minutes.

60
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:31,220
It woke me at night,

61
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:33,080
and it turned ordinary
things,

62
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:34,330
like getting in the car

63
00:01:34,330 --> 00:01:35,550
or up off the couch,

64
00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:37,240
into a decision.

65
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:38,030
After a long

66
00:01:38,030 --> 00:01:40,050
and serious talk with my
husband,

67
00:01:40,050 --> 00:01:42,710
I went back in one more
time.

68
00:01:42,710 --> 00:01:43,980
That was the fourth set

69
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,930
of X-rays on this knee.

70
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:47,470
And like the three before
it,

71
00:01:47,470 --> 00:01:50,020
the answer was everything
looks great.

72
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:51,830
No loosening, no
infection,

73
00:01:51,830 --> 00:01:52,940
nothing wrong.

74
00:01:52,940 --> 00:01:53,840
Only this time there

75
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:55,050
was no new number.

76
00:01:55,050 --> 00:01:57,830
Nobody said give it
another six months.

77
00:01:57,830 --> 00:01:59,550
There was nothing left to
give it.

78
00:01:59,550 --> 00:02:00,650
I sat in the parking lot

79
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:01,940
for a while.

80
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:03,200
Okay, I thought.

81
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,600
Then explain this.

82
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:06,930
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

83
00:02:06,930 --> 00:02:08,510
I hit my breaking point.

84
00:02:08,510 --> 00:02:10,560
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

85
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,030
I had to be

86
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:12,500
in the kitchen by six.

87
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:14,210
Everyone in the house was
asleep

88
00:02:14,210 --> 00:02:15,160
and I was downstairs

89
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:15,800
in the recliner

90
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:16,800
with my leg up,

91
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:18,100
trying to find any angle

92
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:18,850
where it didn't feel

93
00:02:18,850 --> 00:02:19,800
like something was wrapped

94
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:21,750
around my knee and
tightening.

95
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:23,960
My husband didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

96
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:26,620
By then I'd stopped
telling him.

97
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:27,750
And I just thought,

98
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:29,470
is this really my life
now?

99
00:02:29,470 --> 00:02:30,480
I didn't know how many
more

100
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:32,040
school years I had in me.

101
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:33,430
I can't live like this.

102
00:02:33,430 --> 00:02:35,540
So I made myself a
promise.

103
00:02:35,540 --> 00:02:36,310
I wouldn't go a day

104
00:02:36,310 --> 00:02:37,920
without looking for an
answer.

105
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,150
And when I found one,

106
00:02:39,150 --> 00:02:40,180
I'd share it with everyone

107
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:42,120
going through the same
thing.

108
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,980
So I got my laptop out

109
00:02:43,980 --> 00:02:45,010
and went looking.

110
00:02:45,010 --> 00:02:46,260
Not for a product.

111
00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:47,840
For an explanation.

112
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:49,570
Mayo Clinic forums,

113
00:02:49,570 --> 00:02:51,830
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

114
00:02:51,830 --> 00:02:54,720
doctor videos, medical
animations.

115
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:56,000
And that's when I found a
video

116
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,040
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

117
00:02:58,040 --> 00:02:59,340
Steven Salinger,

118
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:00,310
whose own wife had

119
00:03:00,310 --> 00:03:02,090
been through exactly this.

120
00:03:02,090 --> 00:03:03,590
But before I say anything
else,

121
00:03:03,590 --> 00:03:05,470
I want to be straight with
you.

122
00:03:05,470 --> 00:03:07,680
You've already had
something work fast.

123
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:08,700
The ice.

124
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:10,340
The first week of a new
pill.

125
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:12,200
The good day after a
session.

126
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:14,030
Then it wore off.

127
00:03:14,030 --> 00:03:16,160
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

128
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:18,280
Fast relief isn't relief.

129
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,840
It's a preview.

130
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:20,960
So I'm not going

131
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:22,510
to tell you this works
fast.

132
00:03:22,510 --> 00:03:23,440
It doesn't.

133
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:25,430
But if you're willing to
be patient,

134
00:03:25,430 --> 00:03:26,420
and to look at what's
going

135
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:27,700
on around your new knee

136
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:29,120
instead of inside it,

137
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:29,790
there is a real

138
00:03:29,790 --> 00:03:31,610
reason it still hurts.

139
00:03:31,610 --> 00:03:33,500
And something you can do
about it.

140
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:35,050
Let me explain what he
said,

141
00:03:35,050 --> 00:03:35,970
because this is what

142
00:03:35,970 --> 00:03:37,660
changed everything for me.

143
00:03:37,660 --> 00:03:39,350
He started with the
basics.

144
00:03:39,350 --> 00:03:40,500
A knee replacement takes

145
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,160
out the worn joint
surfaces

146
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:44,200
and puts in metal and
plastic.

147
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,670
That's what stops the
arthritis

148
00:03:45,670 --> 00:03:48,230
pain you had before the
operation.

149
00:03:48,230 --> 00:03:50,080
That part I already knew.

150
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:51,730
But then he explained
something

151
00:03:51,730 --> 00:03:53,320
nobody had ever told me.

152
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:54,200
He said,

153
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,050
think about a swollen

154
00:03:55,050 --> 00:03:57,020
foot inside a shoe.

155
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:58,290
The shoe didn't shrink.

156
00:03:58,290 --> 00:04:00,520
Your foot is taking up
more room,

157
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:02,110
so everything feels
cramped

158
00:04:02,110 --> 00:04:04,030
and tight and squeezed.

159
00:04:04,030 --> 00:04:05,080
Your new knee sits

160
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:06,190
in a limited space

161
00:04:06,190 --> 00:04:08,850
with living tissue packed
all around it.

162
00:04:08,850 --> 00:04:10,070
To put that knee in,

163
00:04:10,070 --> 00:04:10,830
the surgeon had

164
00:04:10,830 --> 00:04:12,510
to work through that
tissue.

165
00:04:12,510 --> 00:04:16,310
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

166
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:17,820
At first that's normal.

167
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:19,040
But in some people

168
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,440
that swelling can stay
switched

169
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:22,400
on far longer than
expected.

170
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:24,820
And swollen tissue takes
up more room

171
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:26,430
than calm tissue does.

172
00:04:26,430 --> 00:04:28,820
So when you bend,

173
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:30,550
that tissue gets
compressed.

174
00:04:30,550 --> 00:04:31,670
When you straighten,

175
00:04:31,670 --> 00:04:33,040
it gets pulled tight.

176
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,280
That's the band.

177
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:37,070
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

178
00:04:37,070 --> 00:04:37,910
And you start being

179
00:04:37,910 --> 00:04:39,230
the one who says,

180
00:04:39,230 --> 00:04:40,230
you go ahead.

181
00:04:40,230 --> 00:04:41,360
I'll stay here.

182
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:42,400
And that's exactly why

183
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:43,230
so much of what

184
00:04:43,230 --> 00:04:46,480
I'd tried hadn't worked.

185
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:47,970
Physical therapy
strengthens the

186
00:04:47,970 --> 00:04:49,790
muscles around the knee.

187
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:52,400
Worth doing, and I'd done
it.

188
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:53,420
It does nothing about

189
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:55,120
tissue taking up room.

190
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,610
A nerve block quiets

191
00:04:56,610 --> 00:04:58,720
the nerve carrying the
signal.

192
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:01,360
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

193
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:02,510
But when that irritated

194
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:04,420
tissue finally calms down,

195
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:05,840
it holds less fluid,

196
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:07,630
and it takes up less room.

197
00:05:07,630 --> 00:05:09,140
Less room taken up means

198
00:05:09,140 --> 00:05:11,650
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

199
00:05:11,650 --> 00:05:13,480
That's what takes the
pressure off.

200
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:14,590
After two years of this,

201
00:05:14,590 --> 00:05:16,730
it finally made sense.

202
00:05:16,730 --> 00:05:18,680
The problem was never the
new knee.

203
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,770
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

204
00:05:20,770 --> 00:05:22,620
He calls it the squeeze.

205
00:05:22,620 --> 00:05:23,810
Once you've felt it,

206
00:05:23,810 --> 00:05:25,180
that's the word.

207
00:05:25,180 --> 00:05:26,630
I'd bought knee sleeves,

208
00:05:26,630 --> 00:05:30,070
compression braces,
cushioned work shoes,

209
00:05:30,070 --> 00:05:31,940
a rubber mat for behind
the line,

210
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:34,160
creams, half of Amazon
really,

211
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:35,020
and all any of it

212
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:36,480
gave me was an hour.

213
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,130
I even looked

214
00:05:37,130 --> 00:05:37,960
at going to a clinic

215
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,230
for the light therapy.

216
00:05:39,230 --> 00:05:41,280
But at $200 a session

217
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:43,640
with nothing covered by
insurance,

218
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:45,320
that was a quick no.

219
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:47,200
Then one night I went back

220
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:48,750
to that knee replacement
group

221
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:50,250
and actually read it.

222
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:51,640
Thousands of people,

223
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:53,250
years out from surgery,

224
00:05:53,250 --> 00:05:54,690
comparing notes on
stiffness

225
00:05:54,690 --> 00:05:57,150
and tightness nobody could
explain.

226
00:05:57,150 --> 00:05:59,100
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

227
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:00,870
the same thing kept coming
up.

228
00:06:00,870 --> 00:06:02,080
This one device,

229
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:02,900
and people saying it

230
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:03,700
was the first thing

231
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:05,590
that made a difference.

232
00:06:05,590 --> 00:06:07,650
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

233
00:06:07,650 --> 00:06:09,390
alright, here it comes,

234
00:06:09,390 --> 00:06:10,880
she's selling me
something,

235
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:12,760
let me shut that down
right now.

236
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:13,470
I'm only here

237
00:06:13,470 --> 00:06:15,000
because I made myself a
promise

238
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,620
at 2:30 in the morning

239
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:17,330
that if I ever

240
00:06:17,330 --> 00:06:18,510
found something that
helped,

241
00:06:18,510 --> 00:06:19,680
I'd say so.

242
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,120
It's called the KenRelief

243
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:23,340
Red Light Therapy Wrap.

244
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:25,530
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

245
00:06:25,530 --> 00:06:26,250
It looked like the

246
00:06:26,250 --> 00:06:27,890
cheap knee sleeves off
Amazon

247
00:06:27,890 --> 00:06:29,520
that did nothing for me.

248
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:31,490
But I went to their
website anyway,

249
00:06:31,490 --> 00:06:32,180
just to see what

250
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:33,550
all the fuss was about.

251
00:06:33,550 --> 00:06:34,950
It's the same red light
therapy

252
00:06:34,950 --> 00:06:37,720
clinics charge $200 a
session for,

253
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:40,560
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

254
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:41,440
in a wrap you plug

255
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:43,370
into the wall at home.

256
00:06:43,370 --> 00:06:45,080
Two hundred and forty
lights.

257
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:46,840
Red at 660 nanometers

258
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:49,150
and near-infrared at 850,

259
00:06:49,150 --> 00:06:51,220
run together for the
strongest effect.

260
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:52,710
Four strength levels.

261
00:06:52,710 --> 00:06:54,440
A five to thirty minute
timer.

262
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:55,960
Then I saw the guarantee.

263
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:57,140
Ninety days.

264
00:06:57,140 --> 00:06:58,890
Results or your money
back,

265
00:06:58,890 --> 00:07:01,230
no questions, no store
credit,

266
00:07:01,230 --> 00:07:03,500
and you don't even send it
back.

267
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:04,890
No physical therapist ever

268
00:07:04,890 --> 00:07:06,090
gave me ninety days

269
00:07:06,090 --> 00:07:07,360
to change my mind.

270
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:08,840
There wasn't much to lose,

271
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:09,980
so I ordered it.

272
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:11,480
Two of them, actually.

273
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:13,330
Only the right knee was
replaced,

274
00:07:13,330 --> 00:07:15,230
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

275
00:07:15,230 --> 00:07:15,870
and I'd done it

276
00:07:15,870 --> 00:07:16,700
on a tile floor

277
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:18,070
for two years.

278
00:07:18,070 --> 00:07:20,320
The left one was carrying
the difference.

279
00:07:20,320 --> 00:07:21,280
When it came,

280
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:23,160
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

281
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:24,140
because I'd been let down

282
00:07:24,140 --> 00:07:26,500
too many times to get
excited.

283
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:27,940
What I felt was warmth.

284
00:07:27,940 --> 00:07:29,840
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

285
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:30,840
More like it was coming

286
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:32,160
from inside the knee

287
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,580
and spreading around it.

288
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:34,700
And that was it.

289
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:36,830
That was the whole
experience.

290
00:07:36,830 --> 00:07:38,070
When I took it off,

291
00:07:38,070 --> 00:07:39,600
I'll be honest,

292
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:41,330
nothing dramatic had
happened.

293
00:07:41,330 --> 00:07:43,150
And after what that video
said,

294
00:07:43,150 --> 00:07:45,120
that's exactly what I
expected.

295
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:46,990
What was different was

296
00:07:46,990 --> 00:07:47,920
that for the first time

297
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:49,520
in two years I'd done
something

298
00:07:49,520 --> 00:07:50,510
for my knee

299
00:07:50,510 --> 00:07:51,910
instead of to it.

300
00:07:51,910 --> 00:07:54,130
Twenty minutes, in my own
chair,

301
00:07:54,130 --> 00:07:55,140
after work.

302
00:07:55,140 --> 00:07:57,240
No drive, no copay.

303
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,870
They say twenty minutes.

304
00:07:58,870 --> 00:08:00,060
I did thirty,

305
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:01,140
twice a day,

306
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:03,350
lowest setting that first
week.

307
00:08:03,350 --> 00:08:04,580
Once before work,

308
00:08:04,580 --> 00:08:06,200
once after supper.

309
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:07,010
The first week,

310
00:08:07,010 --> 00:08:08,170
I couldn't have told you

311
00:08:08,170 --> 00:08:10,000
if anything was happening.

312
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:10,610
I tried not

313
00:08:10,610 --> 00:08:11,900
to get my hopes up.

314
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:12,770
I'd had things help

315
00:08:12,770 --> 00:08:14,580
for a week and then stop.

316
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:15,430
But somewhere in the

317
00:08:15,430 --> 00:08:16,730
second week I noticed

318
00:08:16,730 --> 00:08:17,860
I'd come down the stairs

319
00:08:17,860 --> 00:08:19,840
without holding the rail.

320
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:21,350
I hadn't decided to.

321
00:08:21,350 --> 00:08:22,670
I just did it,

322
00:08:22,670 --> 00:08:26,330
then stopped halfway down
because I realized.

323
00:08:26,330 --> 00:08:27,020
By the end of the

324
00:08:27,020 --> 00:08:28,570
fourth week I'd slept
through

325
00:08:28,570 --> 00:08:30,720
the night four times
running.

326
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:31,860
I stood at the counter

327
00:08:31,860 --> 00:08:33,470
and finished making dinner

328
00:08:33,470 --> 00:08:35,680
without looking for the
stool.

329
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:37,050
None of that is dramatic.

330
00:08:37,050 --> 00:08:37,890
All of it was gone

331
00:08:37,890 --> 00:08:39,120
for two years.

332
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,500
A few weeks later my

333
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:41,660
husband asked if I wanted

334
00:08:41,660 --> 00:08:42,460
to walk the long

335
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:44,180
way around the block.

336
00:08:44,180 --> 00:08:45,150
And for the first time

337
00:08:45,150 --> 00:08:46,180
in two years,

338
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:47,540
I said yes.

339
00:08:47,540 --> 00:08:49,150
I wanted to understand
why,

340
00:08:49,150 --> 00:08:50,730
so I read the whole thing.

341
00:08:50,730 --> 00:08:52,540
It comes down to four
steps.

342
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:53,330
One.

343
00:08:53,330 --> 00:08:54,350
The tissue around a new

344
00:08:54,350 --> 00:08:55,970
knee can stay inflamed
long

345
00:08:55,970 --> 00:08:58,130
after surgery is over.

346
00:08:58,130 --> 00:08:58,850
Two.

347
00:08:58,850 --> 00:09:00,980
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

348
00:09:00,980 --> 00:09:02,020
so it takes up more room

349
00:09:02,020 --> 00:09:03,240
than it should.

350
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:04,680
Three.

351
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:06,470
There's only so much room
in there.

352
00:09:06,470 --> 00:09:08,010
Bending compresses it.

353
00:09:08,010 --> 00:09:09,700
Straightening pulls it
tight.

354
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:11,530
That's the squeeze.

355
00:09:11,530 --> 00:09:12,400
Four.

356
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:15,040
Red and near-infrared
light have been studied

357
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:16,700
for calming that
inflammation,

358
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:17,720
so the swelling and the

359
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,400
pressure can come down
with it.

360
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:21,080
In a randomized trial,

361
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:22,490
patients given light
therapy

362
00:09:22,490 --> 00:09:24,990
after a knee replacement
had less pain,

363
00:09:24,990 --> 00:09:27,200
less swelling and better
early movement

364
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:29,020
than those who weren't.

365
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:31,400
A 2025 review said the
same,

366
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:32,380
and was clear the

367
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:33,980
evidence is still limited.

368
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:35,030
I probably sound like a

369
00:09:35,030 --> 00:09:36,370
broken record to my family

370
00:09:36,370 --> 00:09:38,250
and my kitchen crew.

371
00:09:38,250 --> 00:09:39,320
But after two years of

372
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:40,980
doing everything I was
told

373
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:42,410
and getting nowhere,

374
00:09:42,410 --> 00:09:43,650
you have no idea what it's

375
00:09:43,650 --> 00:09:45,650
like to sleep through the
night,

376
00:09:45,650 --> 00:09:47,020
say yes to the walk,

377
00:09:47,020 --> 00:09:48,500
and get my life back.

378
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,340
So take it from me.

379
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:51,830
Don't spend another year
waiting

380
00:09:51,830 --> 00:09:53,030
for it to settle.

381
00:09:53,030 --> 00:09:55,020
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

382
00:09:55,020 --> 00:09:56,390
More than ten thousand
people

383
00:09:56,390 --> 00:09:57,460
with pain after a knee

384
00:09:57,460 --> 00:09:59,600
replacement have already
tried this.

385
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:01,510
Some had it worse than I
did.

386
00:10:01,510 --> 00:10:02,930
You can get the KenRelief
wrap

387
00:10:02,930 --> 00:10:04,080
from their website,

388
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:05,300
with a discount link

389
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:07,980
and ninety days to try it.

390
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:09,640
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

391
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:10,900
you get your money back

392
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:12,520
and you keep the wrap.

393
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:13,250
They only release

394
00:10:13,250 --> 00:10:14,810
so many at that price.

395
00:10:14,810 --> 00:10:16,190
If it's still there,

396
00:10:16,190 --> 00:10:18,334
get one, and stop the
squeeze.

